# The uncaught twin of unit_null_receive_path_catch: a field read through a letter binding holding nothing (the second
# take of a one-letter inbox is 0: author, Q10), no handler -- the implicit `interpreter` throw leaves the method and the
# unit; R0 is stopped (Fails 1, Stopped 1, Thrown 4), exactly as for an own reference holding nothing
# (unit_null_struct_deref_uncaught).  Natively and with the method walked.
MainLetter:
    char: []: []: mainArgs
end: MainLetter

fn: second () int
    receiveMessage: junk MainLetter
    receiveMessage: m MainLetter
    if: m\sender = 0
        return: 2
    return: 3
end: second

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: second(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
